  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Minor Changes\n\n- `RequestActivation` gained an overload taking an `ActivationMethod`, so the browser-based activation request can now ask for an offline license with `RequestActivation(ActivationMethod.Offline)`; existing calls are unchanged. The product has to allow offline activations and the license that fulfils the request needs an offline-capable seat, and fulfilling it with a trial still gives an online license. ([#241](https://github.com/Manevann/moonbase/pull/241))\n- A store that has closed now throws `StoreClosedException` from every licensing call that reaches Moonbase, where it used to surface as a `LicenseInvalidException` or an `HttpRequestException`, or leave `GetRequestedActivation` polling forever. It is deliberately not a `LicenseInvalidException`: treat it like being offline, keep the stored license and validate it locally, as the README's \"Validate on startup\" shows, while devices already activated get a signed offline license and keep working. A `catch (LicenseInvalidException)` no longer sees a closed store, so catch `StoreClosedException` where you catch failures to reach Moonbase. ([#239](https://github.com/Manevann/moonbase/pull/239))\n\n### Patch Changes\n\n- `ErrorType` gains `CaptchaRequired`. A store can now require a captcha on sign-up, which an app cannot show, so for such a store `Register` throws a `UserAuthenticationException` saying so: send the customer to the store's sign-up page in a browser instead. ([#193](https://github.com/Manevann/moonbase/pull/193))",
